# Build output and the corpora cargo-fuzz manages.
target/
corpus/
artifacts/
coverage/

# This is a nested workspace of its own, so `cargo check` in here writes a second
# lock file. It was never tracked, and it should not be: the root `Cargo.lock` is
# tracked because it pins what ships, and nothing here ships. Left untracked and
# unignored, `git add -A` collects it -- which happened on 2026-08-21 and nearly
# put a machine-local dependency state into a commit about something else.
Cargo.lock
